   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><font color=\"#000000\">Hi there, </font></span><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Hope everyone&#39;s project goes well in this stage:)</span><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><font color=\"#000000\" style=\"font-size:12.8px\">I&#39;m the student of GSoC this year from Taiwan. Here is my project link: </font><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\" style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B6hlTfwl1uGWT21wTWRkd3pJWjA/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B6hlTfwl1uGWT21wTWRkd3pJWjA/view?usp%3Dsharing&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792351514880000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1cVbWBPTeHK3p7b-beOe7m\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B6hlTfwl1uGWT21wTWRkd3pJWjA/view?usp=sharing</a>.</span></font><span style=\"font-size:12.8px;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> I am, at first, refactoring some charting functions to use plot.xts (from on xts_0.10-0). But </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12.8px\">I&#39;ve run into a little problem and not yet find a solution. If anyone is available, please kindly give me some advice.</span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\">When I was checking the modified PerformanceAnalytics package by calling R CMD check, I found that, in the output of examples, the charting functions having been refactored to use plot.xts created a new plotting window that would cause the next chart to plot outside of the plotting area. Here is a quick example, </span><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div></span><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;font-size:13px;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;color:rgb(57,51,24);word-wrap:normal;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">library(PerformanceAnalytics) # dependent on xts_0.10-0\r\ndata(edhec)\r\nplot.xts(edhec[, 1])\r\nplot(1:10, rnorm(10))\r\nabline(v=1)</span></code></pre></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><img src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/QebFug8BUFNkmElTsSYz9tB4Z_v7oKDKXcoxZtfjEoNBJN8McSS00vqsRUYd5o-o-8hESBvsYi8s5zrx4QNzMcAJd_PHWIwk9ufD-txI7wUc1wXeE7iYxtMtQHAObAiFr_Z9JSaqUyRK-1IoNKEGa0DBYwJTKVso0o8mxlOcVH-JWA1bgYErm8NLyvFf_jTWwspwulhttm7LRoKuX-yRlhxltvpD5g7TcFxQmiA-qWflJ8LDQfyzaQkZpqRhggbCJ1D2pAUel8FFMnpv4QEqiVnUMMHDHF62vKmBHkYEhMHusqagriHE6hOL2_wf6AlCGIQkqggzGm54Qw3E2jKloiYJ9JHjqc6ojL9QT3D8-AKB8WsUdqpdeGyq3qrARt8-ATmeuBdvJ7uswgPp23quN58KK-yLQlx8bh30k5SKl_Pc-MFOXjyylr6Yw7xGlc9Vug8LrAxMHsPHbGI=s0-d-e1-ft#https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/?ui=2&amp;ik=f3490d4423&amp;view=fimg&amp;th=1552b251ea63b588&amp;attid=0.1&amp;disp=emb&amp;realattid=ii_1552b1c0ffd1292f&amp;attbid=ANGjdJ85DVIaJ1qVWMNAElKR9bZYyBFK7ZhNX3KEVQlU4gyFsSlLax4KzTDsCAfj1Hgcvn1OITpIYPi06h1yFJP0VlHmXegcJ-wKkCiELaC3u79qn4waFkaVLtCzEls&amp;sz=w944-h488&amp;ats=1465454127624&amp;rm=1552b251ea63b588&amp;zw&amp;atsh=1\" alt=\"Inline image 1\" width=\"472\" height=\"244\" style=\"outline:0px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">As you can see the vertical line is beyond the plotting area. I&#39;ve tried to set </span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54);font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\">par(xpd=FALSE)</span><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"> but when the plot object created by plot.xts was wrapped in the function, the plot object would not be returned if I put </span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54);font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;font-size:13px;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\">par(xpd=FALSE)</span><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"> after the plot object. For example,  </span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;font-size:13px;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;color:rgb(57,51,24);word-wrap:normal;background-color:rgb(239,240,241)\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">f &lt;- function(R){\r\n  p &lt;- plot.xts(R)\r\n  p\r\n  par(xpd=FALSE)\r\n}\r\nf(edhec[, 1])</span></code></pre></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">This is what happened actually: </span><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B6hlTfwl1uGWS0J2Wks1bTZGVE0/view?usp=sharing\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);font-size:12.8px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B6hlTfwl1uGWS0J2Wks1bTZGVE0/view?usp%3Dsharing&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792351514880000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2LaCpohwQ7ND9YYnzDyslP\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B6hlTfwl1uGWS0J2Wks1bTZGVE0/view?usp=sharing</a><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">. </span><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">I&#39;m still working on it.</span><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Any suggestion will be appreciated. Thanks in advance.</span><br></div></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\">Best wishes,</div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\">Eric</div></div>"
    ]
